# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 7 — Entity Specifications

---

# Purpose

Part 3 defined which business entities exist.

This section defines **everything about each entity**.

For every entity, this document specifies purpose, ownership, participants, fields, relationships, statuses, allowed and forbidden actions, lifecycle, business rules, audit fields, derived data, dependencies, deletion rules, and visibility rules.

This section is intentionally non-technical.

It is nearly a complete data specification written in product language.

Every workflow, state machine, calculation, permission, notification, screen, and acceptance criterion must conform to these entity definitions.

If the application stores, displays, or behaves differently than this document, the application is incorrect.

---

