# 1. Business

## Purpose

Represents a legally registered organisation using DigiSwasthya as either a Pharmacy or a Stockist.

A Business is the root owner of nearly every other operational entity in the platform.

## Owner

The Business itself.

The Platform Administrator governs verification and suspension, but does not own the business.

## Participants

- Business Owner (primary account holder)
- Business Staff (users belonging to the business)
- Platform Administrator (verification and governance only)

## Required Fields

- Business Name
- Business Type (Pharmacy or Stockist)
- Registered Address
- Contact Phone
- Contact Email
- GST Number
- Drug License Number
- Owner Name
- Registration Status
- Verification Status
- Account Status (Active, Suspended, Deactivated)
- Created At
- Created By

## Optional Fields

- Trade Name / Brand Name
- Alternate Phone
- Website
- Business Description
- Logo
- Service Areas (Stockist)
- Delivery Settings
- Bank Account Details
- Additional Licenses
- Notes
- Preferred Language
- Business Preferences

## Relationships

- Has many Users
- Has one current Business Verification
- Has many Connections
- Pharmacy may create many Orders
- Stockist may receive many Orders
- Stockist owns one Product Catalogue
- Owns Inventory
- Owns Addresses
- Owns Support Tickets
- Owns Notifications (business-scoped)
- Owns financial history associated with the business

## Valid Statuses

- Draft Registration
- Pending Verification
- Verified
- Verification Rejected
- Documents Requested
- Suspended
- Reactivation Pending
- Deactivated

## Allowed Actions

- Register
- Submit verification documents
- Update profile (where permitted)
- Invite staff
- Manage staff
- Manage settings
- Request reactivation (if suspended and allowed)
- View own business records

## Forbidden Actions

- Approve own verification
- Change business type after verification without platform process
- Delete financial history
- Access another business's private data
- Trade while unverified
- Trade while suspended

## Lifecycle

```
Draft Registration
        ↓
Pending Verification
        ↓
Verified  ←→  Suspended  →  Reactivation Pending  →  Verified
        ↓
Verification Rejected / Documents Requested
        ↓
Resubmission → Pending Verification
```

Deactivated is a terminal or near-terminal business state requiring administrator process.

## Business Rules

- A business must be either Pharmacy or Stockist, never both in the current product.
- Only verified and active businesses may trade.
- GST and Drug License must be unique where platform uniqueness rules apply.
- Business records survive user deletion.
- Suspension immediately blocks trading capabilities.
- Historical transactions remain visible after suspension.

## Audit Fields

- Created At
- Created By
- Updated At
- Updated By
- Suspended At
- Suspended By
- Suspension Reason
- Reactivated At
- Reactivated By
- Verification Decision History

## Derived Data

- Total Orders
- Total Invoices
- Outstanding Balance
- Active Connections Count
- Staff Count
- Last Activity At

## Dependencies

- At least one User (owner) to operate
- Valid identity and license information for verification

## Deletion Rules

- A Business must never be hard-deleted if it has financial or transactional history.
- Deactivation is preferred over deletion.
- Related historical Orders, Invoices, Payments, Returns, and Credit Notes must be retained.
- Staff users may be deactivated; business history remains.

## Visibility Rules

- Business sees its own profile and operational data.
- Connected trading partners see only permitted public/trading profile fields.
- Platform Administrator can view all businesses for governance.
- Unconnected businesses see only discoverable public profile fields.

