# 2. User

## Purpose

Represents an individual person who accesses DigiSwasthya on behalf of exactly one Business.

## Owner

The Business to which the user belongs.

## Participants

- The User
- Business Owner / Manager (staff administration)
- Platform Administrator (support and account governance where required)

## Required Fields

- Full Name
- Phone Number
- Email (if required by registration flow)
- Password / Authentication Credential Reference
- Belonging Business
- Role Within Business
- Account Status (Active, Invited, Suspended, Removed)
- Created At

## Optional Fields

- Profile Photo
- Alternate Phone
- Designation
- Permissions Override Set
- Last Login At
- Device Preferences
- Notification Preferences

## Relationships

- Belongs to exactly one Business
- May create or act on Orders, Payments, Returns, Messages, Support Tickets according to permissions
- Receives Notifications
- May be assigned Deliveries (Delivery staff)

## Valid Statuses

- Invited
- Active
- Suspended
- Removed / Deactivated

## Allowed Actions

- Log in (if Active)
- Update own profile (permitted fields)
- Perform capabilities granted by role/permissions
- Reset password
- Log out

## Forbidden Actions

- Belong to multiple businesses simultaneously
- Transfer ownership of business records to themselves personally
- Access data outside granted permissions
- Delete audit history
- Approve platform-level verification

## Lifecycle

```
Invited
   ↓
Active
   ↓
Suspended ←→ Active
   ↓
Removed / Deactivated
```

## Business Rules

- Every user belongs to exactly one business.
- Removing a user must never delete business records they created.
- Actions remain attributed to the user who performed them, even after removal.
- Owner role cannot be removed without transferring ownership.
- Suspended users cannot perform business actions.

## Audit Fields

- Created At
- Created By
- Updated At
- Updated By
- Last Login At
- Suspended At
- Suspended By
- Removed At
- Removed By
- Role Change History

## Derived Data

- Permissions Effective Set
- Open Tasks Count
- Unread Notifications Count
- Last Activity At

## Dependencies

- Must reference an existing Business
- Invitation flow depends on inviter permissions

## Deletion Rules

- Users are deactivated/removed, not erased.
- Historical attribution must remain.
- Personal login access is revoked on removal.
- Messages and actions remain as business records.

## Visibility Rules

- User can view own profile.
- Business admins can view staff list and roles.
- Trading partners do not see internal staff lists unless a specific operational view requires a contact person.
- Platform Administrator may view users for support and governance.

