# 3. Business Verification

## Purpose

Represents the verification state and evidence used to decide whether a Business may trade on DigiSwasthya.

## Owner

Platform Administrator (decision ownership).

Business owns the submitted documents and application.

## Participants

- Business Owner / authorised business user
- Platform Administrator

## Required Fields

- Business Reference
- Verification Status
- Submitted Documents
- Submitted At
- Current Reviewer (when under review)
- Decision (when decided)
- Decision At (when decided)

## Optional Fields

- Reviewer Notes
- Correction Requests
- Resubmission Count
- Risk Flags
- Internal Comments

## Relationships

- Belongs to one Business
- References uploaded documents
- Influences Business Account Status and trading eligibility

## Valid Statuses

- Not Started
- Submitted
- Under Review
- Documents Requested
- Approved
- Rejected

## Allowed Actions

- Submit documents
- Resubmit after correction request
- Admin request documents
- Admin approve
- Admin reject
- View status

## Forbidden Actions

- Business approving itself
- Trading before approval
- Editing locked approved verification evidence without a controlled amendment process
- Deleting verification history

## Lifecycle

```
Not Started
     ↓
Submitted
     ↓
Under Review
     ↓
Documents Requested → Resubmitted → Under Review
     ↓
Approved / Rejected
```

## Business Rules

- Every business has exactly one current verification status.
- Approval is required before trade.
- Rejection must include a reason.
- Document requests pause trading eligibility until resolved.
- Previous verification decisions remain in history.

## Audit Fields

- Submitted At
- Submitted By
- Reviewed At
- Reviewed By
- Decision
- Decision Reason
- Document Request History

## Derived Data

- Days Pending
- Resubmission Count
- Verification Completeness Score (if used)

## Dependencies

- Business must exist
- Required documents must be present before approval

## Deletion Rules

- Verification records are never deleted.
- Document replacement creates history, not silent overwrite without trace.

## Visibility Rules

- Business sees status, required actions, and non-internal reasons.
- Platform Administrator sees full verification record including internal notes.
- Other businesses never see verification documents.

