# 7. Inventory

## Purpose

Represents physical stock available to a Business, maintained at batch level and aggregated by product.

## Owner

The Business that holds the stock.

- Stockist inventory for sale/fulfilment
- Pharmacy inventory for internal stock management

## Participants

- Business inventory managers
- Fulfilment staff (stockist)
- Delivery confirmation flows may adjust received stock (pharmacy)

## Required Fields

- Business
- Product
- Batch
- Quantity On Hand
- Quantity Reserved
- Quantity Available (or derivable)
- Last Movement At

## Optional Fields

- Location / Rack
- Reorder Level
- Reorder Quantity
- Notes

## Relationships

- Belongs to Business
- References Product
- References Batch
- Affected by Orders, Deliveries, Returns, Adjustments

## Valid Statuses

- Available
- Reserved
- Low Stock
- Expired
- Quarantined
- Zero

Status may be derived from quantities and batch expiry.

## Allowed Actions

- Add stock
- Adjust stock
- Reserve stock
- Release reservation
- Consume stock on dispatch/delivery rules
- Receive stock
- Quarantine stock
- View history

## Forbidden Actions

- Manual negative stock
- Selling expired sellable stock
- Changing another business's inventory
- Silent inventory edits without movement reason

## Lifecycle

Inventory quantity changes through recognised movements:

```
Stock In
Reservation
Reservation Release
Dispatch / Sale Consumption
Return In
Adjustment
Expiry / Quarantine
```

## Business Rules

- Inventory must never become negative.
- Available = On Hand − Reserved (subject to final calculation rules).
- Expired batches are not sellable.
- Every quantity change must reference a movement reason and source document where applicable.
- Reservations occur according to order acceptance/allocation rules.

## Audit Fields

- Movement At
- Movement By
- Movement Type
- Source Document
- Previous Quantity
- New Quantity
- Reason

## Derived Data

- Available Quantity
- Reserved Quantity
- Expiry Risk Quantity
- Low Stock Flag
- Inventory Value

## Dependencies

- Product
- Batch
- Business

## Deletion Rules

- Inventory records are not deleted; they move to zero and remain in history through movements.
- Batch expiry does not erase history.

## Visibility Rules

- Owning business sees full inventory.
- Trading partners do not see exact internal stock unless product availability exposure is explicitly configured.
- Platform Administrator may view for investigations.

