# 8. Batch

## Purpose

Represents a manufacturing batch of a product with quantity, batch identity, and expiry.

## Owner

Business that holds/created the batch record (typically Stockist for sellable stock; Pharmacy for received stock records).

## Participants

- Inventory managers
- Fulfilment staff

## Required Fields

- Product
- Batch Number
- Expiry Date
- Quantity
- Owning Business
- Batch Status
- Created At

## Optional Fields

- Manufacturing Date
- Manufacturer
- Supplier Reference
- MRP at Receipt
- Cost
- Location
- Recall Flag
- Notes

## Relationships

- Belongs to Product
- Underpins Inventory
- Referenced by Order allocation / Invoice lines / Delivery lines / Return lines where batch tracking applies

## Valid Statuses

- Active
- Expired
- Quarantined
- Recalled
- Consumed / Closed

## Allowed Actions

- Create batch
- Update quantity through movements
- Mark quarantined
- Mark recalled
- View expiry
- Consume on fulfilment

## Forbidden Actions

- Deliver expired batch as sellable goods
- Reuse batch identity incorrectly for a different product within the same business stock model
- Delete batch with movement history

## Lifecycle

```
Active
  ↓
Quarantined / Recalled / Expired
  ↓
Consumed / Closed
```

## Business Rules

- Expiry belongs to batch, not product.
- Expired batches cannot be newly allocated for fulfilment.
- Recall immediately blocks sellable allocation.
- Returned goods may return into quarantined or sellable stock based on return disposition rules.

## Audit Fields

- Created At / By
- Updated At / By
- Status Change History
- Recall History

## Derived Data

- Days to Expiry
- Expiry Percentage / Risk Band
- Remaining Sellable Quantity

## Dependencies

- Product
- Owning Business

## Deletion Rules

- Batches with history are closed, not deleted.

## Visibility Rules

- Owning business sees batch detail.
- Pharmacy may see batch/expiry on delivered goods and invoices where provided.
- Unrelated businesses do not see batch stock.

