# 9. Order

## Purpose

Represents a purchase request from a Pharmacy to a Stockist for one or more products.

An Order expresses intent to purchase. It is not itself a financial settlement document.

## Owner

Created by Pharmacy.

Fulfilment owned by Stockist after submission.

## Participants

- Pharmacy (buyer)
- Stockist (seller)
- Authorised staff on both sides
- Delivery staff (operational participation after dispatch)

## Required Fields

- Order Number
- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Connection Reference
- Order Status
- Order Lines (Product, Quantity, Unit Price Snapshot)
- Delivery Address
- Placed At
- Placed By

## Optional Fields

- Notes from Pharmacy
- Notes from Stockist
- Requested Delivery Date
- Rejection Reason
- Cancellation Reason
- Partial Fulfilment Flags
- Internal References
- Expected Dispatch Date

## Relationships

- Belongs to one Pharmacy and one Stockist
- Requires Active Connection at creation
- Contains many Order Lines
- May generate one or more Invoices
- May have one or more Deliveries
- May lead to Returns on delivered items
- Triggers Notifications

## Valid Statuses

- Draft
- Pending
- Accepted
- Rejected
- Cancelled
- Packed
- Dispatched
- Partially Delivered
- Delivered
- Closed

Exact transition rules are defined in State Machines.

## Allowed Actions

- Create / edit draft
- Submit
- Accept
- Reject
- Cancel (when permitted)
- Pack
- Dispatch
- Confirm delivery / receive
- View / track
- Duplicate / reorder from history

## Forbidden Actions

- Pharmacy accepting its own order
- Ordering without Active connection
- Editing after locked fulfilment states
- Deleting an order with financial/delivery history
- Exceeding business rules for quantities/cancellations

## Lifecycle

```
Draft
  ↓
Pending
  ↓
Accepted / Rejected / Cancelled
  ↓
Packed
  ↓
Dispatched
  ↓
Partially Delivered / Delivered
  ↓
Closed
```

## Business Rules

- Order must contain at least one line.
- Quantities must be greater than zero.
- Price snapshots are captured at relevant commitment points.
- No financial liability exists until invoicing rules create it.
- Inventory reservation occurs according to acceptance/allocation rules.
- Historical order integrity cannot be rewritten silently.

## Audit Fields

- Created At / By
- Submitted At / By
- Accepted At / By
- Rejected At / By
- Cancelled At / By
- Status Change History
- Line Change History before lock

## Derived Data

- Order Subtotal
- Tax Total
- Order Total
- Fulfilled Quantity
- Outstanding Quantity
- Linked Invoice Count
- Payment Status Summary

## Dependencies

- Verified Pharmacy
- Verified Stockist
- Active Connection
- Sellable Products

## Deletion Rules

- Drafts may be discarded according to rules.
- Submitted and later orders are never hard-deleted.
- Cancellation closes the order; it remains visible.

## Visibility Rules

- Pharmacy and Stockist on the order can view it.
- Platform Administrator can view for support/governance.
- Other businesses cannot view it.

