# 10. Invoice

## Purpose

Represents the financial document defining what a Pharmacy owes a Stockist for fulfilled/billable goods.

## Owner

Stockist (issuer)

## Participants

- Stockist
- Pharmacy
- Accountant roles on either side
- Platform Administrator (read-only governance/support)

## Required Fields

- Invoice Number
- Related Order
- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Invoice Lines
- Invoice Date
- Subtotal
- Tax Total
- Grand Total
- Invoice Status
- Outstanding Amount
- Created At
- Created By

## Optional Fields

- Due Date
- Discount Total
- Round Off
- Notes
- Payment Terms
- Credit Note Applications
- Attachment / PDF Reference

## Relationships

- Originates from Order
- May be linked to Delivery
- Settled by one or more Payments
- Adjusted by Credit Notes (without rewriting invoice history)
- Belongs to Pharmacy–Stockist pair

## Valid Statuses

- Draft
- Issued
- Partially Paid
- Paid
- Overdue
- Cancelled / Void (only under strict rules)
- Locked

## Allowed Actions

- Create from eligible fulfilment
- Issue
- View
- Record payment allocation against
- Apply credit note against outstanding
- Mark overdue (system or rules)
- Void only under controlled pre-settlement rules

## Forbidden Actions

- Pharmacy editing stockist invoice totals
- Silent rewrite of issued financial lines
- Deleting an issued invoice
- Creating invoice without valid order/fulfilment basis
- Paying more than allowed without explicit overpayment rules

## Lifecycle

```
Draft
  ↓
Issued
  ↓
Partially Paid ←→ Paid
  ↓
Overdue (from Issued / Partially Paid when past due)
  ↓
Locked
```

Void/Cancel only from eligible early states under strict rules.

## Business Rules

- Invoice is the source of financial liability.
- Payments never modify immutable issued invoice lines; they reduce outstanding balance.
- Credit notes reduce liability via application, not by editing original lines.
- Invoice numbering must be unique per stockist.
- Issued invoices become permanent financial records.

## Audit Fields

- Created At / By
- Issued At / By
- Voided At / By / Reason
- Status Change History
- Allocation History References

## Derived Data

- Outstanding Amount
- Paid Amount
- Credit Applied Amount
- Days Overdue
- Settlement Status

## Dependencies

- Order
- Active/valid trading relationship at creation time
- Billable quantities

## Deletion Rules

- Issued invoices are never deleted.
- Draft invoices may be discarded before issue.
- Void retains record with reason.

## Visibility Rules

- Issuing Stockist and billed Pharmacy can view.
- Platform Administrator can view.
- Unrelated parties cannot view.

