# 11. Payment

## Purpose

Represents money paid by a Pharmacy toward one or more Invoices.

## Owner

Created by Pharmacy (payment submission).

Confirmation/approval owned by Stockist.

## Participants

- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Accountant roles
- Platform Administrator (oversight)

## Required Fields

- Payment Number / Reference
- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Amount
- Payment Method
- Payment Date
- Payment Status
- Created At
- Created By

## Optional Fields

- Transaction Reference
- Payment Proof Attachment
- Notes
- Allocated Invoice List
- Hold Reason
- Rejection Reason
- Received Bank Account

## Relationships

- Belongs to Pharmacy and Stockist
- Allocated to one or more Invoices
- May interact with Credit Note application rules
- Triggers Notifications
- Affects Outstanding Balance

## Valid Statuses

- Draft
- Submitted
- Under Review
- Approved
- Rejected
- On Hold
- Cancelled

## Allowed Actions

- Create payment
- Submit proof
- Allocate to invoices
- Approve
- Reject
- Place on hold
- View history

## Forbidden Actions

- Approving own payment as pharmacy
- Deleting approved payment history
- Allocating to unrelated invoices
- Changing approved payment amount silently
- Using payment to rewrite invoice documents

## Lifecycle

```
Draft
  ↓
Submitted
  ↓
Under Review
  ↓
Approved / Rejected / On Hold
  ↓
(On Hold → Under Review / Approved / Rejected)
```

## Business Rules

- Payment reduces outstanding only when Approved (unless explicit rules say otherwise).
- Allocation total cannot exceed payment amount.
- Allocation cannot exceed invoice outstanding at allocation time.
- Duplicate payment references should be detected and blocked or flagged.
- Rejected payments create no settlement effect.

## Audit Fields

- Created At / By
- Submitted At / By
- Reviewed At / By
- Approved At / By
- Rejected At / By
- Hold History
- Allocation History

## Derived Data

- Unallocated Amount
- Allocated Amount
- Settlement Effect on each invoice

## Dependencies

- At least one payable Invoice or explicit advance-payment rule
- Valid Pharmacy–Stockist relationship context

## Deletion Rules

- Financial payments are not deleted.
- Drafts may be discarded.
- Rejected/cancelled remain for audit.

## Visibility Rules

- Pharmacy and Stockist in the payment can view.
- Platform Administrator can view.
- Others cannot.

