# 13. Return

## Purpose

Represents a request to return delivered products and seek approval for physical and financial adjustment.

## Owner

Initiated by Pharmacy.

Approval owned by Stockist.

## Participants

- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Inventory staff
- Accountant (credit issuance side)

## Required Fields

- Return Number
- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Source Order / Delivered Items
- Return Lines (Product, Quantity, Reason)
- Return Status
- Created At
- Created By

## Optional Fields

- Notes
- Evidence Attachments
- Pickup Details
- Rejection Reason
- Disposition (Restock, Quarantine, Destroy)

## Relationships

- References delivered Order items
- May reference Invoice lines
- Approved returns may generate Credit Notes
- May adjust Inventory based on disposition

## Valid Statuses

- Draft
- Submitted
- Under Review
- Approved
- Partially Approved
- Rejected
- Goods Received Back
- Closed

## Allowed Actions

- Create return request
- Submit
- Review
- Approve / partially approve
- Reject
- Record goods received back
- Issue credit note from approval
- View status

## Forbidden Actions

- Returning undelivered items
- Returning quantities above delivered quantities
- Returning after eligibility window if such window exists
- Pharmacy approving its own return
- Financial adjustment without approval

## Lifecycle

```
Draft
  ↓
Submitted
  ↓
Under Review
  ↓
Approved / Partially Approved / Rejected
  ↓
Goods Received Back (if physical return required)
  ↓
Closed
```

## Business Rules

- Returns do not immediately change payments.
- Only approved returns create credit eligibility.
- Returned quantity ≤ delivered quantity for each item.
- Inventory impact depends on disposition.
- Closed returns remain permanent records.

## Audit Fields

- Created At / By
- Submitted At / By
- Reviewed At / By
- Decision
- Decision Reason
- Goods Received At / By
- Disposition History

## Derived Data

- Requested Value
- Approved Value
- Credit Issued Value
- Pending Review Age

## Dependencies

- Delivered goods
- Original Order
- Active enough trading context to process returns (even if new orders are blocked, historical returns may still be processed under rules)

## Deletion Rules

- Returns are not deleted after submission.
- Drafts may be discarded.

## Visibility Rules

- Pharmacy and Stockist participants can view.
- Platform Administrator can view.
- Others cannot.

