# 14. Credit Note

## Purpose

Represents financial credit issued to a Pharmacy, typically after an approved return or authorised adjustment.

## Owner

Stockist (issuer)

## Participants

- Stockist
- Pharmacy
- Accountant roles

## Required Fields

- Credit Note Number
- Pharmacy
- Stockist
- Source Reference (Return / Adjustment)
- Amount
- Credit Note Status
- Remaining Amount
- Issued At
- Issued By

## Optional Fields

- Related Invoice References
- Notes
- Expiry of Credit (if policy exists)
- Line-level breakdown
- Reason Code

## Relationships

- Originates from Approved Return or authorised adjustment
- Applies against future or outstanding Invoice liabilities
- Does not rewrite historical invoice documents

## Valid Statuses

- Draft
- Issued
- Partially Applied
- Fully Applied
- Cancelled / Void (strict rules)
- Expired (if policy exists)

## Allowed Actions

- Create from approved source
- Issue
- Apply to invoices
- View
- Void only under strict unapplied rules

## Forbidden Actions

- Issuing credit without approved source
- Exceeding approved return value
- Pharmacy creating stockist credit notes
- Editing issued credit amount silently
- Using credit as cash refund unless future product explicitly supports refunds

## Lifecycle

```
Draft
  ↓
Issued
  ↓
Partially Applied → Fully Applied
  ↓
Expired / Void (conditional)
```

## Business Rules

- Credit notes reduce future/outstanding liabilities.
- Remaining amount cannot be negative.
- Application cannot exceed remaining credit or invoice outstanding.
- Historical invoices remain intact; application is separate.

## Audit Fields

- Created At / By
- Issued At / By
- Voided At / By / Reason
- Application History

## Derived Data

- Remaining Credit
- Applied Credit
- Related Outstanding Reduction

## Dependencies

- Approved Return or authorised adjustment source
- Pharmacy–Stockist context

## Deletion Rules

- Issued credit notes are never deleted.
- Drafts may be discarded.

## Visibility Rules

- Issuing Stockist and recipient Pharmacy can view.
- Platform Administrator can view.
- Others cannot.

