# 16. Message

## Purpose

Represents conversational communication between platform users or businesses.

Messages assist coordination. They do not replace official business workflows.

## Owner

Sender owns the sent message content.

Conversation is shared between participants.

## Participants

- Sender User / Business
- Recipient User / Business
- Support participants where applicable

## Required Fields

- Conversation / Thread Reference
- Sender
- Recipient(s)
- Message Body
- Sent At
- Message Status

## Optional Fields

- Attachments
- Related Entity Reference (Order, Invoice, etc.)
- Edited At
- Deleted For Sender Flag

## Relationships

- May reference Order / Invoice / Return context
- Belongs to participants
- Independent from official status changes

## Valid Statuses

- Sent
- Delivered
- Read
- Deleted for Sender
- Removed for Policy Violation (admin)

## Allowed Actions

- Send message
- Read message
- Attach file where permitted
- Link to business context
- Report message

## Forbidden Actions

- Treating a message as an official approval
- Editing business records through messaging
- Messaging outside allowed participant relationships (e.g., unconnected trade chat if restricted)

## Lifecycle

```
Sent
  ↓
Delivered
  ↓
Read
```

Moderation may remove visibility without erasing audit where required.

## Business Rules

- A message saying "Approved" does not approve an order/payment/return.
- Official decisions occur only through official capabilities.
- Message history should remain available for dispute context according to retention rules.

## Audit Fields

- Sent At / By
- Read At
- Moderation Actions

## Derived Data

- Unread Thread Count
- Last Message Preview

## Dependencies

- Valid participants
- Optional related entity visibility permissions

## Deletion Rules

- User-side delete may hide from self; conversation audit may remain.
- Business-critical moderation retains evidence as required.

## Visibility Rules

- Only conversation participants can view.
- Platform Administrator may view for dispute/safety support.
- Unrelated users cannot view.

