# 18. Analytics (Derived Entity)

## Purpose

Represents calculated business insights derived from authoritative records.

Analytics are never the source of truth.

## Owner

Derived for a Business or for Platform Administrator (global).

## Participants

- Pharmacy users (pharmacy analytics)
- Stockist users (stockist analytics)
- Platform Administrator (platform analytics)

## Required Fields

- Scope (Business / Platform)
- Metric Name
- Period
- Calculated Value
- Calculated At
- Source Definition Reference

## Optional Fields

- Dimensions (product, supplier, customer, route)
- Comparison Period Value
- Filters Applied

## Relationships

- Derived from Orders, Invoices, Payments, Inventory, Returns, Connections, etc.
- Never replaces underlying entities

## Valid Statuses

- Current
- Stale
- Recalculating

## Allowed Actions

- View
- Filter
- Export authorised analytics
- Recalculate (system)

## Forbidden Actions

- Editing analytics as if primary records
- Using analytics to overwrite operational data

## Lifecycle

```
Calculated → Available → Stale → Recalculated
```

## Business Rules

- Underlying records always win in case of conflict.
- Definitions of metrics must match Business Calculations.
- Exports are snapshots, not new sources of truth.

## Audit Fields

- Calculated At
- Definition Version
- Exported At / By (for export actions)

## Derived Data

Not applicable beyond the metrics themselves.

## Dependencies

- Source transactional entities
- Metric definitions from Business Calculations

## Deletion Rules

- Analytics snapshots may be regenerated.
- Source data retention is independent and authoritative.

## Visibility Rules

- Businesses see only their own analytics.
- Platform Administrator sees platform-wide analytics.
- No cross-business private analytics leakage.

