# Cross-Entity Integrity Rules

The following must always remain true across entities.

1. Every transactional entity references valid Pharmacy and Stockist where applicable.
2. Orders require Active Connection at creation.
3. Invoices require a valid order/fulfilment basis.
4. Payments allocate only to eligible invoices.
5. Returns reference only delivered quantities.
6. Credit Notes originate from approved adjustments.
7. Inventory never goes negative.
8. Expired batches are not newly supplied.
9. Notifications and Messages never replace official workflow decisions.
10. User deletion never deletes Business history.
11. Historical financial documents are immutable in substance.
12. Derived analytics never override source records.

